{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 29, :comments ["<b>And if a man sells a dwelling house of a walled city</b> — because selling one's house is very hard in a person's eyes, and he is ashamed of it at the time he sells it, the Torah wanted that he may redeem it within the first year. And because a man works a field and from it bread comes forth for his sustenance, He wanted that the field go out in the Jubilee. But a house, after the despair — that he has changed his dwelling and has remained a year in another house — does not harm him, for his sustenance is not diminished if it is permanently removed. And the houses of the courtyards are made for guarding the fields and to serve as dwelling for those who work the land, and therefore their law is like the field of the land."], :book :leviticus, :voice :ramban, :lang :en, :chapter 25, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-22T04:00:22.287300129Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}